Opt-in kill switch for vLLM 0.23's TRTLLM-gen attention on SM100 (B200-class):
a colocated rollout EngineCore can futex-deadlock on idle/resume when TRTLLM
attention is active. No behavior change unless VLLM_DISABLE_TRTLLM_ATTN=1.

SCOPE: vLLM 0.23 environments only. The hunk is generated against 0.23's
vllm/utils/flashinfer.py and does NOT apply to vLLM 0.11, and stock vLLM (any
version) never reads VLLM_DISABLE_TRTLLM_ATTN at all — the variable only does
something once this patch is applied. So exporting it in the vLLM 0.11 training
env has no effect, and no equivalent patch is shipped for 0.11.

NOTE: the comment text inside the added block was corrected after this patch
shipped. A venv patched with the ORIGINAL file cannot be reverse-applied with
this one (the reverse hunk no longer matches the applied bytes) — retrieve the
original with `git show c1ad157:patches/vllm023-disable-trtllm-attn.patch`, or
just delete the [J-Zero patch] block by hand. Applied behavior is identical.

Apply:  cd <venv>/lib/python3.12/site-packages && patch -p1 < this-file
Revert: cd <venv>/lib/python3.12/site-packages && patch -R -p1 < this-file

--- a/vllm/utils/flashinfer.py
+++ b/vllm/utils/flashinfer.py
@@ -357,6 +357,16 @@
     if envs.VLLM_BATCH_INVARIANT:
         return False
 
+    # [J-Zero patch] Opt-in kill switch for the TRTLLM-gen attention backend.
+    # A colocated rollout EngineCore can futex-deadlock on idle/resume during
+    # the reward stage (~30s pauses) when TRTLLM attention is active on SM100.
+    # Standard FlashInfer attention is stable. This patch is for vLLM 0.23
+    # only. Default behavior is UNCHANGED (TRTLLM on) unless
+    # VLLM_DISABLE_TRTLLM_ATTN=1. Revert: re-apply in reverse (patch -R -p1).
+    import os as _os
+    if _os.environ.get("VLLM_DISABLE_TRTLLM_ATTN", "0") == "1":
+        return False
+
     # Requires SM100 and NVIDIA artifactory to be accessible to download cubins
     return (
         current_platform.is_device_capability_family(100) and has_nvidia_artifactory()
